      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dale City was founded in 1960 by real estate developer Cecil Don Hylton, who named the community after the rolling hills and dales of the Piedmont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://ohmyfacts.com/world/cities/30-facts-about-dale-city/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hylton\u2019s company, Hylton Enterprises, began in Dale City in 1960 and built over 22,000 homes, shaping the town\u2019s suburban landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dale_City%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The streets of Dale City alphabetically line up from east to west along Dale Boulevard, starting with Ashdale and ending at Trentdale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dale_City%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Dale City\u2019s first sewer and cable television services were launched by Hylton, making it a pioneer in local utilities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dale_City%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Russell House and Store on Minnieville Road dates back to the early 19th century, long before Dale City\u2019s modern development.",
